        "original_id": "6d6aa377-ac71-5aba-ab36-d2d1556cf0fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Simon Bloom\n- Companies: Universal Pictures\n- People: Carl Laemmle, Mark Dintenfass, Charles O. Baumann, Adam Kessel, Pat Powers, William Swanson, David Horsley, Robert H. Cochrane, Jules Brulatour\n- Concepts: bidding war, manuscript, film studios\n\nFacts:\n- In 1912, Universal Pictures was founded by Carl Laemmle, Mark Dintenfass, Charles O. Baumann, Adam Kessel, Pat Powers, William Swanson, David Horsley, Robert H. Cochrane, and Jules Brulatour.\n- Universal Pictures is the oldest surviving film studio in the United States, the world's fourth-oldest film studio after Gaumont, Pathé, and Nordisk Film, and the oldest in terms of the overall film market.\n- The first Simon Bloom book was optioned by Universal Pictures after a bidding war over its manuscript.",
